WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.658 --> 00:00:03.658
Our Universe is a mystery.

00:00:03.795 --> 00:00:05.440
It's a collection of mysteries.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.000
The more we learn,
the more we realise

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.720
that there’s a lot more
that we do not know.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.080
Here are five big mysteries.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.880
There is no reason to believe

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.480
that our Universe is unique.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.320
It is quite possible that just
as our Universe was created,

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.760
many universes were also created.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.240
If that is the case, then we live,

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.560
not in a single Universe,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.480
but in a vast collection
of universes

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.840
that physicists refer to
as the multiverse.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:52.200
We can think of those
as island universes -

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.440
each with its own quirks,

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.840
maybe even each
with its own laws of physics.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:02.920
For example, there could be
one of these other universes

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:08.880
where gravity is 100 times stronger
than it is in our Universe.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:13.080
If we could somehow
prove conclusively

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:17.040
the existence of multiple universes,
of the multiverse,

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:21.280
that would be a genuine
intellectual revolution -

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:24.200
a complete change
in our cosmic thinking.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:32.880
The dark side of the Universe
is a really big mystery.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.080
The dark matter
and the dark energy

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:40.840
make up no less than 96%
of what the Universe contains.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.400
The stuff that you and I,
the Sun, the Earth,

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.960
the stars, the galaxies are made of,

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.720
that is just the icing on the cake.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:55.160
It makes up only 4%
of what our Universe contains.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.560
The most likely explanation
for the dark matter is that

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:02.720
it is made up of some exotic
fundamental particle

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.880
that came into existence
just a tiny fraction of a second

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.080
after our Universe was formed
in the Big Bang.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:12.880
But it is a mystery.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.240
We have compelling evidence
that it's there.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.520
We suspect
it's a fundamental particle.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.600
But, frustratingly,
it has yet to be discovered.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.560
I think most people have heard
about black holes.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.920
Fewer may have heard about
white holes.

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:41.280
White holes are in a way
the opposite of a black hole.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.120
Black holes eat everything.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.360
White holes kind of
vomit everything out.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.320
Nothing can come out
of a black hole.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.560
Nothing can go into
a white hole.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.000
Whether white holes exist
or not

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:00.040
is a matter of heated debate.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:04.880
Of course, if they do exist,
they are fascinating,

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.640
and they may even raise the possibility

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:12.360
that they act as tunnels
to other universes,

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.920
or indeed to other epochs
in our own Universe.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.920
But they remain
hypothetical objects.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.200
The current view in cosmology

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:29.080
is that everything we see
in the Universe - everything -

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:33.640
started life as something called
a quantum fluctuation.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.640
Sounds mysterious.
Let me explain what this is.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:41.240
When the Universe was born,
it expanded very rapidly

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:45.640
in a very short period of time
known as "cosmic inflation".

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.600
As the Universe expanded,

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:50.480
these quantum fluctuations
were stretched,

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:57.080
and this stretching seeded the Universe
with tiny ripples.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:01.800
These ripples yet
are the origin of galaxies,

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.480
galaxy clusters, planets,
the Earth, and people.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:11.200
The mystery here is,
is it really possible

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:15.960
that a sub-microscopic entity
like a quantum fluctuation

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.400
could eventually grow
into the Milky Way galaxies?

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:24.880
If you had told me that a few years
ago, I would have thought,

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:27.080
"You're really out of your mind."

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.320
And yet today, the standard model

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:35.280
of the formation of cosmic structure
is exactly what I just described.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:42.600
Time fascinates, not just physicists,

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:44.600
it fascinates everyone.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:49.000
And yet, it is a relative concept.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:56.000
For example, if you travel
faster and faster and faster,

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.480
time slows down
more and more and more.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:03.640
If you travel at the speed
of light, time simply stops.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:06.760
If you look at the equations
of physics,

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.720
it is striking that time can go
forwards or backwards -

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:13.520
the equations of physics
don’t distinguish.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:16.000
Because of this,
many people believe

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.160
that you can travel into the past,

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:21.440
because there is nothing
in the equations of physics

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.840
that forbids you doing that.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:27.480
It is quite possible that we could
in principle travel back in time,

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:32.720
so long as we do not introduce
any inconsistency with the future.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:38.760
So that’s five big cosmic mysteries.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:42.840
But each mystery -
as is always the case in science -

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.560
leads to another, even bigger, mystery.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:51.000
And we haven’t even got to possibly
the biggest mystery of them all -

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:53.760
are we alone in the Universe?

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.960
But that’s a whole new story.

